Here’s a complete, implementation-agnostic **feature specification & architecture plan** you can hand to an AI agent (or developer) later. It’s structured phase-by-phase, includes safety/performance constraints, and defines exactly what “done” looks like for each module.

---
## 🎯 PROJECT OVERVIEW
- **Goal**: A modular admin tools mod for Minecraft
- **Scope**: Server-authoritative commands + client-side management UIs + debug utilities
- **Design Principle**: Safe by default, toggleable per feature, zero vanilla command override, explicit permission gating
- **Target**: Version & loader agnostic (agent will adapt to Forge/Fabric/NeoForge based on your choice)

---
## 🏗️ CORE ARCHITECTURE BLUEPRINT
| Layer | Responsibility | Implementation Notes |
|-------|----------------|----------------------|
| **Permission Gate** | Centralized `hasAdminAccess(Player)` check | OP status or custom permission node. Blocks all admin actions if false. |
| **Command Router** | Single root command with subcommands | Prevents namespace pollution. Routes to feature modules. |
| **Event Bus** | Registers commands, GUIs, tick events, config reloads | One-time setup in mod init. No runtime feature registration. |
| **Data Sync** | Server → Client state for GUIs | Use network packets or vanilla sync APIs. Never trust client data. |
| **Logger** | Action audit trail | Chat + file log. Timestamp, admin, action, target, result. |

---
## 📦 FEATURE MODULES (PHASED)

### 🔹 PHASE 1: MVP COMMANDS (Core Management)
| Command | Purpose | Input/Output | Safety Rules | Scope |
|---------|---------|--------------|--------------|-------|
| `/admintools tp &lt;target&gt;` | Teleport admin to player | Player name | Target must be online. Coords validated against world border. | Server |
| `/admintools tp &lt;x&gt; &lt;y&gt; &lt;z&gt;` | Teleport to coords | 3 numbers | Within world bounds. Blocks solid collision check before spawn. | Server |
| `/admintools give &lt;player&gt; &lt;item&gt; [amount]` | Spawn items | Player, item ID, optional count | Max 64k per stack. No NBT injection. | Server |
| `/admintools gamemode &lt;mode&gt; [player]` | Change game mode | Creative/Survival/Spectator | Defaults to executor. Spectator prevents interaction. | Server |
| `/admintools time set &lt;value&gt;` | Set world time | 0-24000 or day/night | Clamped to valid range. Broadcasts change. | Server |
| `/admintools weather &lt;clear/rain/thunder&gt;` | Change weather | Enum | Prevents thunder in nether/end. | Server |
| `/admintools kill &lt;target&gt;` | Remove entity/player | Player or entity | Requires confirmation prompt. Logs action. | Server |

**Done Criteria**: All commands parse correctly, reject invalid input, respect permissions, log actions, and never crash servers.

---

### 🔹 PHASE 2: GUI MANAGEMENT TOOLS
| Tool | Purpose | UI/UX Flow | Data Source | Safety |
|------|---------|------------|-------------|--------|
| **Player Inventory Viewer** | Browse any online player’s inventory | Click player → opens read-only screen | Server-side `PlayerInventory` | No edit mode. Show only. |
| **Entity Inspector** | View stats, NBT, effects of any entity | Right-click entity → opens panel | `Entity` + `CompoundTag` | Read-only. Edit buttons disabled by default. |
| **Player Manager** | Ban/kick/warn with reason logging | Search player → action buttons → reason input | Server player list + ban list | Requires confirmation. Logs reason. |
| **Chunk Manager** | View/modify chunk state | Click chunk → shows entity/block counts → clear buttons | `LevelChunk` + `BlockEntity` | Clear limited to entities/blocks. No world generation. |

**Done Criteria**: GUIs open smoothly, sync data server→client, prevent manipulation, and close cleanly. No memory leaks on repeat opens.

---

### 🔹 PHASE 3: DEBUG & WORLD UTILITIES
| Tool | Purpose | Trigger/Interface | Output/Effect | Safety |
|------|---------|-------------------|---------------|--------|
| **Debug Overlay** | Real-time world stats | Toggle key | FPS, chunk coords, entity count, lag spikes, loaded chunks | Read-only. Doesn’t affect performance. |
| **Block/Entity Picker** | Copy block/entity data | Left-click block, right-click entity | Shows ID, state, NBT preview | No direct modification. Copy to clipboard or log. |
| **World Edit Brush (Light)** | Replace/fill areas | Command + cursor selection | Sphere/cylinder fill, replace, copy/paste | Undo stack limited to 20. No structure corruption. |
| **Performance Cleaner** | Remove lag sources | GUI toggle: clear armor stands, items, falling blocks | Removes entities matching filter | Optional range limit. Requires confirmation. |

**Done Criteria**: Tools provide accurate data, respect world boundaries, and never cause chunk unloads or server ticks to drop below 19ms.

---

### 🔹 PHASE 4: POLISH & COMPATIBILITY
- **Waypoint System**: Save/load teleport coordinates with GUI list
- **Command Fallback**: Gracefully degrade if vanilla commands fail
- **Mod Integration Hooks**: Optional compatibility with popular mods (e.g., `jei`, `cloth-config`)
- **Sound/Feedback**: Subtle UI sounds, progress bars for long operations
- **Localization Ready**: All strings externalized for translation

---
## 🔒 SAFETY & COMPLIANCE LAYER
| Rule | Implementation |
|------|----------------|
| **Permission Gate** | All admin actions blocked if `!hasAdminAccess()` |
| **Destructive Confirmation** | Kill, clear, replace, world edit require 2-step approval |
| **Rate Limiting** | Max 10 commands/sec per player. Spam triggers cooldown |
| **World Safety** | No chunk generation, no nether/end weather changes, bounds checking |
| **NBT Safety** | Read-only NBT access. No tag injection. Max depth 5 for parsing |
| **Thread Safety** | All world/player modifications on main thread. GUIs on client thread |

---
## ⚙️ CONFIGURATION & UX DESIGN
- **Config Structure**:
  - `enable_debug_overlay: true`
  - `enable_entity_inspector: true`
  - `max_command_rate: 10`
  - `log_actions_to_file: true`
  - `permission_mode: op | custom`
  - `custom_permission_node: admin.tools.use`
- **UX Principles**:
  - Dark theme, high contrast
  - Tooltips on hover
  - Clear success/failure messages
  - No auto-execution without confirmation
  - Graceful error messages (not stack traces)

---
