Here’s a complete, consolidated summary of your admin tools mod. It’s structured as a single reference document you can hand directly to an AI agent or developer for implementation.

---
## 📦 MOD OVERVIEW
- **Concept**: Admin & Staff Oversight Tools Mod
- **Core Philosophy**: Server-authoritative, safe by default, zero vanilla command replacement, config-driven, audit-focused
- **Target**: Singleplayer, local SMP, dedicated servers
- **Design Constraints**: No chunk/block modification, no client-side cheating, performance-safe, anti-cheat compatible, version/loader agnostic

---
## 🔑 ROLE & PERMISSION SYSTEM
- **In-Game Commands**: `/adminrole assign &lt;player&gt; &lt;role&gt;`, `/adminrole grant &lt;player&gt; &lt;feature&gt;`, `/adminrole remove &lt;player&gt; &lt;feature&gt;`, `/adminrole list`, `/adminrole reset &lt;player&gt;`
- **OP Behavior**: Vanilla OPs automatically bypass all role restrictions and receive full access
- **Feature Gating**: Each role gets a defined list of allowed features (`invsee`, `endersee`, `xrayreport`, `modify_mode`, `audit_view`, `staff_alerts`, `spectator_stealth`, etc.)
- **Colored Prefixes**: `[COLOR][ROLE] playername` applied to chat, nametags, and tab list
- **Config Control**: Role definitions, colors, prefixes, and display toggles are hot-reloadable
- **Offline Support**: Roles persist across disconnects via UUID-based storage

---
## 📖 CORE FEATURES

### 1. Inventory & Ender Chest Viewers
- **Commands**: `/invsee &lt;player&gt;`, `/endersee &lt;player&gt;`
- **GUI Layout**:
  - Inventory: Double chest (54 slots) + armor/offhand/metadata panel
  - Ender Chest: Single chest (27 slots)
- **Behavior**: 
  - Read-only for lower roles
  - OPs & `modify_mode` roles can edit items (auto-logged)
  - Offline players load from JSON files
  - No rate limits, no vanilla command overlap
  - Modded items display basic ID/count; NBT shown read-only

### 2. Chest Interaction Tracker (Owner-Only CSV)
- **Behavior**: Silent background process logging every interaction with chest-type blocks (chests, barrels, shulkers, hoppers, droppers, dispensers, furnaces, etc.)
- **Access**: **Strictly file-only.** No in-game commands, no GUI, no staff permissions. Only the server owner accesses it via file explorer/FTP.
- **CSV Format**:
  ```csv
  Date,Time,Player,Coordinates,Block_Broken,Items Added,Items Removed
  2024-05-01,12:38:33,Aguga2201,(128|64|-52),false,"192 gold_ingot, 6 oak_log",""
  2024-05-01,12:39:10,Aguga2201,(128|64|-52),true,"",""
  ```
  - `Coordinates`: Single string in exact `(X|Y|Z)` format
  - `Block_Broken`: strictly `true` or `false` (lowercase, unquoted)
  - `Items Added/Removed`: comma-separated item lists, quoted only if containing commas
  - Only logs rows where items were actually added/removed OR block was broken
- **File Management**: `config/admin-tools/chest_tracker.csv` → UTF-8, append-only, 50MB cap (FIFO), flush 30s/shutdown, single async writer thread

### 3. X-Ray / Automation Heuristic Detector
- **Detection Method**: Behavioral tracking, not block modification
- **Metrics**: Block break rate, torch/light placement ratio, ore exposure %, chunk update frequency, movement patterns (straight-line mining, AFK tunneling, rapid reloads)
- **Dimension-Specific Rules**: Configurable thresholds per dimension (`overworld`, `the_nether`, `the_end`, plus custom biome fallback)
- **Output**: Risk score (0-100), timeline of events, `/xrayreport &lt;player&gt;` for staff breakdown
- **Performance**: Lightweight, event-driven, no world scanning, FPS impact &lt;2%

### 4. Staff-First Alert System
- **Flow**: 
  1. Score crosses `warning_threshold` → private message to all staff/OPs
  2. Fixed 10-second delay begins
  3. Delay completes → public broadcast to all players
- **Non-Dismissable**: No cancel commands. Staff get a heads-up to prepare/investigate, but the alert fires automatically
- **Cooldown**: Prevents repeated alerts for the same player (configurable, default 5 mins)
- **Messages**: Fully customizable via config. Staff and public formats separate
- **Logging**: Both steps recorded in audit trail

### 5. Occlusion Overlay (Admin Debug Tool)
- **Purpose**: Visual aid for admins to see what players can/can't see
- **Behavior**: Darkens/tints blocks outside player light radius or behind occluding geometry using renderer hooks
- **Rendering**: Client-side overlay only. No block state changes, no texture packs, no rendering breaks
- **Controls**: Toggleable via config or command, dimension-aware, performance-capped
- **Permission**: `admin.occlusion_overlay` or OP-only

### 6. Spectator Stealth
- **Purpose**: Hide spectator status from regular players while preserving admin debugging
- **Behavior**: 
  - Spoofs game mode & metadata packets to non-admins
  - Skips ghost transparency & spectator UI rendering
  - Normal nametag & entity model shown
  - Server logic unchanged (still flies/noclips/can't interact)
- **Admin Override**: `admin.see_spectators` role can toggle reveal mode to see true spectator status
- **Safety**: Packet spoofing only affects non-admin clients. Zero desync risk. Anti-cheat friendly

---
## 🛡️ SAFETY & COMPLIANCE LAYER
- **Permission Gate**: Centralized `hasFeatureAccess(player, feature)` check. All admin actions blocked if false
- **Destructive Safeguards**: Modify mode auto-logs all changes. No item injection, no NBT manipulation
- **Thread Safety**: Server reads on main thread, GUI updates on client thread, async file I/O on dedicated writer thread
- **Memory/Performance**: GUIs dispose on close, overlay releases GPU resources, no cached player data beyond session
- **Anti-Cheat Friendly**: No packet manipulation for players, no chunk generation, no invisible entities, movement smoothing optional via config

---
## 📁 CONFIGURATION & LOGGING
- **Main Config**: `config/admin-tools/config.json`
  - Role definitions & permissions
  - Heuristic thresholds per dimension
